WEBVTT

00:00:35.202 --> 00:00:37.996
Air date, unknown.

00:00:38.121 --> 00:00:40.207
The impossible has happened.

00:00:40.332 --> 00:00:44.044
It would take days
to recount the events I've witnessed.

00:00:44.169 --> 00:00:46.880
So, settle in.
It all began...

00:00:47.005 --> 00:00:50.008
Quiet, you! This court-martial
is now in session.

00:00:50.133 --> 00:00:52.886
The honorably sexy
Zapp Brannigan residing.

00:00:53.011 --> 00:00:54.888
Bring in the accused.

00:00:57.224 --> 00:00:59.393
Oh, my.

00:00:59.518 --> 00:01:02.312
Philip J. Fry,
you stand accused

00:01:02.437 --> 00:01:05.232
of traveling to the forbidden
planet Omega 3,

00:01:05.357 --> 00:01:08.944
a crime punishable by 12
concurrent death sentences.

00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:13.115
- Do you understand the charges?
- One beep for "yes," two beeps for "no."

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:16.994
Yes. So noted. Do you plead guilty?

00:01:17.119 --> 00:01:21.331
Double yes. Guilty!

00:01:21.456 --> 00:01:24.168
I will now
carry out the sentence. Kif, my gun.

00:01:24.293 --> 00:01:26.170
Wait!
He pled "not guilty."

00:01:26.295 --> 00:01:28.338
Order!
Order in the court!

00:01:28.463 --> 00:01:33.510
Very well then, Mr. Fry. Please recount
the events that led you to be guilty.

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:43.562
The professor said he was taking
a brief nap,

00:01:43.645 --> 00:01:45.355
so we only have time for six movies.

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:48.567
Let's take these six Jim Carrey movies
and record over them!

00:01:48.692 --> 00:01:51.361
You know what six movies average out
to be really good?

00:01:51.445 --> 00:01:53.238
The first six Star Trek movies!

00:01:53.363 --> 00:01:57.075
Everybody hit the deck!

00:01:57.201 --> 00:01:59.328
Shh!
Those words are forbidden.

00:01:59.453 --> 00:02:02.122
What words? Star Trek?

00:02:02.247 --> 00:02:03.957
- Shh!
- Shut your gills!

00:02:05.209 --> 00:02:08.170
That sound. It's patrol car 718! Hide him!

00:02:18.263 --> 00:02:20.140
The court is intrigued.

00:02:20.265 --> 00:02:22.893
Perhaps we could hear more
about these forbidden words

00:02:23.018 --> 00:02:26.605
from someone with
a sexily seductive voice.

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:30.817
With pleasure. You see, the show was
banned after the Star Trek wars.

00:02:30.943 --> 00:02:33.278
You mean the vast migration
of Star Wars fans?

00:02:33.403 --> 00:02:35.989
Uh, no. That was
the Star Wars trek.

00:02:38.367 --> 00:02:40.827
By the 23rd century,
Star Trek fandom

00:02:40.953 --> 00:02:45.249
had evolved from a loose
association of nerdswith skin problems

00:02:45.374 --> 00:02:47.793
into a full-blown religion.

00:02:47.918 --> 00:02:50.796
And Scotty beamed them
to the Klingon ship

00:02:50.921 --> 00:02:53.173
where they would
be no Tribble at all.

00:02:53.298 --> 00:02:56.343
All power
to the engines.

00:02:56.468 --> 00:02:59.179
As country after country
fellunder its influence,

00:02:59.304 --> 00:03:02.891
world leaders became threatened
by the movement's power.

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:05.227
And so the Trekkies
were executed

00:03:05.352 --> 00:03:07.896
in the manner
most befitting virgins.

00:03:08.021 --> 00:03:10.232
- Whoa!
- He's dead, Jim.

00:03:10.357 --> 00:03:13.861
He's dead, Jim.
He's dead, Jim.

00:03:13.986 --> 00:03:16.947
Finally, the sacred texts
were banned.

00:03:18.532 --> 00:03:22.452
The last copies of
the 79episodes and six movies

00:03:22.578 --> 00:03:26.290
were dumped on the
forbidden world Omega 3,

00:03:26.415 --> 00:03:30.919
along with that blooper reel
where the door doesn'tclose all the way.

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:34.298
Thus, Star Trek was forever
scoured from human memory.

00:03:34.423 --> 00:03:38.385
Another classic science-fiction show
canceled before its time.

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:41.305
Tsk, tsk, tsk.
I've never heard of such a brutal

00:03:41.430 --> 00:03:44.391
and shocking injustice
that I cared so little about.

00:03:44.516 --> 00:03:48.437
- Next witness!
- Bender the Robot, please take the stand.

00:03:49.688 --> 00:03:52.524
She's all yours, buddy.

00:03:52.649 --> 00:03:55.360
I'd only met
the defendant, Fry, once,

00:03:55.485 --> 00:03:57.529
but I knew
he was up to no good.

00:03:57.654 --> 00:04:00.365
- Please use the beeps.
- Oh!

00:04:04.578 --> 00:04:08.749
Mr. Nimoy! I came as soon
as I heard what happened centuries ago.

00:04:08.874 --> 00:04:10.751
I can't believe
your show was banned.

00:04:10.876 --> 00:04:14.171
I have absolutely
no idea what you're talking about.

00:04:16.381 --> 00:04:19.176
You know... 1966?

00:04:19.301 --> 00:04:21.762
Seventy-nine episodes?
About 30 good ones?

00:04:21.887 --> 00:04:26.141
Oh, really. I've done too many things
to remember one particular TV series.

00:04:26.266 --> 00:04:28.352
But if... If you want to
discuss my books of poetry...

00:04:28.477 --> 00:04:30.145
Come on! Remember that episode

00:04:30.229 --> 00:04:32.356
where you got high on spores
and smacked Kirk around?

00:04:32.481 --> 00:04:36.985
No. Perhaps you're thinking of my
one-man show about Vincent van Spock.

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:39.404
I... I... I mean van Gogh.
Damn!

00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:41.365
Aha!
You can't escape it.

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:44.451
Oh, you're right.

00:04:44.576 --> 00:04:46.787
I can't.

00:04:46.912 --> 00:04:49.957
Uh...
Geez, don't get upset.

00:04:50.082 --> 00:04:52.167
I mean, okay,
I outwitted you, but...

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:55.170
No. It's my
fellow cast members.

00:04:55.295 --> 00:04:58.757
Three hundred years ago,
they left Earth behind.

00:05:02.553 --> 00:05:05.556
This planet doesn't
appreciate us anymore, Leonard.

00:05:05.631 --> 00:05:10.177
Bill, you are,
and always shall be, my friend.

00:05:10.302 --> 00:05:12.930
But I just signed
a six-month lease on my apartment.

00:05:13.055 --> 00:05:15.307
I can't walk away from
a commitment like that.

00:05:15.432 --> 00:05:18.018
Farewell, my friend.

00:05:18.143 --> 00:05:20.354
Oh!

00:05:27.528 --> 00:05:31.740
Why did the world turn its back
on our obvious greatness?

00:05:31.865 --> 00:05:34.326
I'm literally
angry with rage!

00:05:34.451 --> 00:05:35.702
Your costars may be gone,

00:05:35.786 --> 00:05:39.456
but we can still get those episode tapes
back for the whole world to see!

00:05:39.581 --> 00:05:41.458
Come on!

00:05:41.583 --> 00:05:43.377
Yes! Front row!

00:05:48.423 --> 00:05:50.926
You can't go to Omega 3!

00:05:51.051 --> 00:05:53.137
It's forbidden!
I forbid you!

00:05:53.262 --> 00:05:56.765
But we have to! The world needs Star Trek
to give people hope for the future!

00:05:56.890 --> 00:05:59.351
But it's set 800 years
in the past.

00:05:59.476 --> 00:06:01.311
Yeah! Why is this
so important to you?

00:06:01.436 --> 00:06:03.397
'Cause it...
It taught me so much.

00:06:03.522 --> 00:06:05.524
Like how you should
accept people,

00:06:05.649 --> 00:06:09.862
whether they be black,
white, Klingon, or even female.

00:06:09.987 --> 00:06:13.407
But most importantly,
when I didn't have any friends,

00:06:13.532 --> 00:06:15.617
it... It made me feel
like maybe I did.

00:06:15.742 --> 00:06:19.246
Well, that is
touchingly pathetic.

00:06:19.371 --> 00:06:21.165
I guess I can't
let you go alone.

00:06:21.290 --> 00:06:25.502
I'll go too...
With Leonard's permission, of course.

00:06:29.631 --> 00:06:32.092
We're entering the Omega system.

00:06:32.217 --> 00:06:35.220
Warning. You are nowin forbidden space.

00:06:35.345 --> 00:06:37.306
Forbidden, schur-schmidden.

00:06:37.431 --> 00:06:39.099
What are they gonna do,
write a letter?

00:06:39.224 --> 00:06:41.310
Ooh, I'm so scared.

00:06:41.435 --> 00:06:43.228
I've lost control of the ship!

00:06:43.353 --> 00:06:45.606
Lost control of the ship!

00:06:58.494 --> 00:07:01.038
Oh, dip!

00:07:01.163 --> 00:07:02.915
Dip, indeed.

00:07:08.462 --> 00:07:10.672
It's all stuff from that forbidden show.

00:07:10.798 --> 00:07:14.510
So many cardboard sets.
So many memories.

00:07:14.635 --> 00:07:16.887
- If only the others...
- I guess that's my cue.

00:07:18.847 --> 00:07:21.016
- Bill!
- L-Dog!

00:07:21.141 --> 00:07:23.227
- Hey! This is wonderful!
- Oh, man.

00:07:23.352 --> 00:07:26.939
- I feel like hugging you.
- Well, I would, except you have no body.

00:07:27.064 --> 00:07:29.900
And we're both men.

00:07:30.025 --> 00:07:33.403
Nichelle! George! Walter!

00:07:33.529 --> 00:07:35.697
DeForrest!
Welshie!

00:07:35.823 --> 00:07:36.824
Welshie?

00:07:36.907 --> 00:07:40.494
We did some musical reunion specials
in the 2200s.

00:07:40.619 --> 00:07:43.163
But the guy who played Scotty
had trouble yodeling.

00:07:43.288 --> 00:07:46.625
Ever since then,
Welshie has been a welcome participant

00:07:46.750 --> 00:07:48.377
in our escapades.

00:07:48.502 --> 00:07:50.671
Aye!

00:07:50.796 --> 00:07:53.507
I can't believe it!
How'd you all end up here?

00:07:53.632 --> 00:07:57.511
We were on our way to Welshie's cousin's
house to stay in the guest room

00:07:57.636 --> 00:08:01.974
when our ship was pulled down to this
planet and crashed, just like yours.

00:08:03.475 --> 00:08:05.102
When we woke up,
we had these bodies.

00:08:05.227 --> 00:08:07.855
Say it in Russian.

00:08:07.980 --> 00:08:10.899
Ven vee voke up,
vee had these wah-dies.

00:08:11.024 --> 00:08:13.277
Eee!
Now say nuclear "wessels"!

00:08:13.402 --> 00:08:15.487
- No!
- We love it here.

00:08:15.612 --> 00:08:18.448
Everything is provided for us,
and we never age.

00:08:18.574 --> 00:08:20.534
Check out these abs.

00:08:20.659 --> 00:08:23.537
- Yowza!
- But who's doing all this for you?

00:08:23.662 --> 00:08:26.457
You know, we never thought about it.
We're famous celebrities.

00:08:26.582 --> 00:08:29.918
- We're used to this sort of treatment.
- It is I!

00:08:30.043 --> 00:08:33.505
Whoa! What a cheesy effect!

00:08:33.630 --> 00:08:36.884
I'm not an effect!
You doubt my power?

00:08:37.009 --> 00:08:39.219
I do!

00:08:39.344 --> 00:08:41.722
Aye!

00:08:41.847 --> 00:08:45.809
Welshie!

00:08:53.567 --> 00:08:57.529
This court will now hear some
very sensual testimony

00:08:57.654 --> 00:09:00.491
from this court's ex-lover,
Turanga Leela.

00:09:00.616 --> 00:09:02.618
Go yourself.

00:09:04.828 --> 00:09:06.747
Behold another power,

00:09:06.872 --> 00:09:10.209
different from
the one you saw earlier!

00:09:13.045 --> 00:09:16.673
Hey! A body!
Buff, tan...

00:09:16.799 --> 00:09:18.842
Yeah.
This is mine, all right.

00:09:18.967 --> 00:09:20.719
All right, you gas.
What's the deal?

00:09:20.844 --> 00:09:25.682
Centuries ago, the videotaped adventures
of the Enterprise crew

00:09:25.808 --> 00:09:28.644
rained down upon my planet.

00:09:28.769 --> 00:09:30.938
Over and over
I watched them,

00:09:31.063 --> 00:09:33.649
especially the five
with the energy beings.

00:09:33.774 --> 00:09:38.570
I am Melllvar!
Seer of the Tapes! Knower of the Episodes!

00:09:38.695 --> 00:09:42.574
Tremble before my encyclopedic
knowledge of Star Trek!

00:09:42.699 --> 00:09:44.576
Tremble? I laugh.

00:09:44.701 --> 00:09:46.537
Nobody knows more about Star Trek than me!

00:09:46.620 --> 00:09:48.455
I beg to differ!

00:09:49.998 --> 00:09:53.627
Long have I waited
for the one who played Spock.

00:09:53.752 --> 00:09:56.672
At last we can begin.

00:09:57.631 --> 00:10:00.259
Cool!
A Star Trek convention!

00:10:00.384 --> 00:10:02.636
Uh... Uh, Melllvar?
Can you give us some idea

00:10:02.761 --> 00:10:04.638
of how long
this is going to last?

00:10:04.763 --> 00:10:05.973
Until time stops.

00:10:06.056 --> 00:10:07.766
- What?
- You can't do this!

00:10:07.891 --> 00:10:10.269
Now, we have
a full schedule of events.

00:10:10.394 --> 00:10:13.647
- Uh, can people who hate Star Trek leave?
- Good question.

00:10:13.772 --> 00:10:17.526
No. You have to stay even longer!

00:10:19.820 --> 00:10:22.656
Um... Uh...
Sign it to Melllvar.

00:10:22.781 --> 00:10:24.700
Melllvar has three "L's".

00:10:24.825 --> 00:10:28.829
I think I've done enough conventions
to know how to spell Melllvar.

00:10:30.622 --> 00:10:34.293
- Say "nerd"!
- Nerd!

00:10:34.418 --> 00:10:37.004
I'm Slim Shady.

00:10:37.129 --> 00:10:39.506
Yes.
I'm the real Shady.

00:10:39.631 --> 00:10:43.343
All you other Slim Shadys
are just imitating.

00:10:43.469 --> 00:10:47.681
So, won't the real Slim Shady
please stand up?

00:10:47.806 --> 00:10:50.267
Please stand up.
Please stand up.

00:10:50.392 --> 00:10:53.604
How can you do
a spoken-word version of a rap song?

00:10:53.729 --> 00:10:55.606
He found a way.

00:10:55.731 --> 00:11:00.569
For 100 quatloos, who did the captain
maroon on Ceti Alpha Five?

00:11:00.694 --> 00:11:02.571
Khan!

00:11:02.696 --> 00:11:04.698
Uh, Khan?

00:11:04.823 --> 00:11:07.493
- Correct!
- My button has broken!

00:11:07.618 --> 00:11:10.704
The trivia contest is ended.
I now have a surprise.

00:11:10.829 --> 00:11:13.373
You will perform
a fan script

00:11:13.499 --> 00:11:15.626
written by
the ultimate Trek fan!

00:11:15.751 --> 00:11:20.047
- You have my fan script?
- I meant me! Melllvar's the ultimate fan!

00:11:20.172 --> 00:11:23.509
Oh. I was confused because the scoreboard
says something different.

00:11:23.634 --> 00:11:26.637
Trivia contest over! Take your scripts!

00:11:26.762 --> 00:11:29.556
We have limited
rehearsal time.

00:11:29.681 --> 00:11:31.850
Now, I didn't make enough
copies of the script,

00:11:31.975 --> 00:11:35.103
so George and Walter
will have to share.

00:11:35.229 --> 00:11:37.356
Uh... You probably don't want us

00:11:37.439 --> 00:11:39.983
to see you rehearsing,
or it'll give away the ending.

00:11:40.108 --> 00:11:42.736
That's right!
The ending must not be ruined!

00:11:42.861 --> 00:11:44.571
- We'll go wait in the ship.
- Okay.

00:11:44.696 --> 00:11:47.407
Not till I get
my 600 quatloos!

00:11:50.828 --> 00:11:53.372
This is wrong.
We shouldn't have abandoned them there.

00:11:53.497 --> 00:11:55.499
I don't know.
I'm feelin' pretty good about it.

00:11:55.624 --> 00:11:58.919
I didn't want to leave them either, Fry.
But what were we supposed to do?

00:11:59.044 --> 00:12:02.631
Well, usually on the show, someone would
come up with a complicated plan,

00:12:02.756 --> 00:12:04.633
then explain it
with a simple analogy.

00:12:04.758 --> 00:12:08.804
Hmm. If we can reroute
engine power through the primary weapons

00:12:08.929 --> 00:12:11.598
and reconfigure them
to Melllvar's frequency,

00:12:11.723 --> 00:12:13.976
that should overload
his electro-quantum structure.

00:12:14.101 --> 00:12:16.436
Like putting too much air
in a balloon!

00:12:16.562 --> 00:12:18.814
Of course!
It's so simple!

00:12:21.984 --> 00:12:25.821
"Alas, my ship,
whom I love like a woman,

00:12:25.946 --> 00:12:27.823
"is... Disabled."

00:12:27.948 --> 00:12:31.201
- Oh, Lord.
- "Fascinating, Captain.

00:12:31.326 --> 00:12:33.954
"And logical too.
Yet we need some help."

00:12:34.079 --> 00:12:37.624
"Look, Captain.
Melllvar will help us."

00:12:41.211 --> 00:12:44.381
"Captain, I wope he will
welp our vessel."

00:12:44.506 --> 00:12:46.133
Wessel!

00:12:46.258 --> 00:12:48.010
You're not acting hard enough!

00:12:48.093 --> 00:12:50.596
Melllvar, you have to respect your actors.

00:12:50.721 --> 00:12:53.807
When I directed Star Trek IV, I got
a magnificent performance out of Bill

00:12:53.932 --> 00:12:55.809
because I respected him
so much.

00:12:55.934 --> 00:12:57.811
And when I directed
Star Trek V,

00:12:57.936 --> 00:13:01.899
I got a magnificent performance
out of me because I respected me so much.

00:13:05.486 --> 00:13:09.198
Okay! I'm done "recafoobelling"
the energy-motron!

00:13:09.323 --> 00:13:11.200
Or whatever!

00:13:11.325 --> 00:13:13.410
Fire!

00:13:16.789 --> 00:13:21.418
"My, what a handsome
energy creature you are.

00:13:21.543 --> 00:13:23.879
"I love you."

00:13:24.004 --> 00:13:27.216
Hey, you wrote it!

00:13:34.431 --> 00:13:37.226
It's not working!
He's drawing strength from our weapons!

00:13:37.351 --> 00:13:39.728
Like a balloon, and...
Something bad happens!

00:13:57.287 --> 00:13:57.748
Yep.

00:14:00.374 --> 00:14:02.543
So, uh,
how's rehearsal going?

00:14:02.668 --> 00:14:06.797
Lousy. Here I've been
admiring a bunch of actors, while you,

00:14:06.922 --> 00:14:10.801
a crew of genuine space heroes,
risked your lives to save them.

00:14:10.926 --> 00:14:13.053
Hey, we've done
heroic things too.

00:14:13.178 --> 00:14:15.806
Yeah.
In the third season, I kissed Shatner.

00:14:15.931 --> 00:14:19.434
Silence! My whole world
has turned upside down.

00:14:19.560 --> 00:14:21.436
I have but one option.

00:14:21.562 --> 00:14:23.856
- Keep them and let us go?
- No!

00:14:23.981 --> 00:14:27.568
To determine who is more worthy
of my fanatical devotion,

00:14:27.693 --> 00:14:32.156
I shall pit you against each other
in armed combat... To the death!

00:14:33.991 --> 00:14:36.160
Where'd you get
an idiotic idea like that?

00:14:36.285 --> 00:14:39.955
Episodes 19, 46,
56 and 77!

00:14:40.080 --> 00:14:44.877
Great list.
Except you forgot episode 66.

00:14:45.002 --> 00:14:47.504
I was getting to that one!

00:14:57.723 --> 00:15:00.601
So Melllvar ordered
a battle to the death.

00:15:00.726 --> 00:15:03.187
I assume no one survived?

00:15:03.312 --> 00:15:06.023
Can we get on with this?
My foot's getting tired.

00:15:09.151 --> 00:15:12.070
This will be your standard
battle to the death.

00:15:12.196 --> 00:15:15.282
The only weapons...
Whatever you can find.

00:15:15.407 --> 00:15:17.576
But I warn you.
Do nothing

00:15:17.701 --> 00:15:20.204
until I have signaled
the start of combat.

00:15:21.330 --> 00:15:23.957
Okay, start.

00:15:30.798 --> 00:15:34.009
I don't have much experience at fighting,
except with you guys.

00:15:34.134 --> 00:15:37.387
I have an idea. Wasn't there an episode
where I threw my shoe at the enemy?

00:15:37.513 --> 00:15:40.599
You mean Doohan?

00:15:40.724 --> 00:15:43.352
Whoever it was,
I did it like this. Yaah!

00:15:43.477 --> 00:15:47.022
- Ow!
- My foot's cold.

00:15:48.565 --> 00:15:50.776
There. We can
make these into spears.

00:15:50.901 --> 00:15:54.530
And we can tie these caterpillars together
to make bow strings for bows and arrows.

00:15:54.655 --> 00:15:56.824
And we can use this machine gun
to shoot them!

00:15:56.949 --> 00:15:59.159
Yee-haw!

00:16:06.125 --> 00:16:08.752
That was fun.

00:16:10.212 --> 00:16:13.882
What if I distract them
with my famous fan dance?

00:16:14.007 --> 00:16:16.051
Oh, that's good,
good, good, good. And then, George,

00:16:16.176 --> 00:16:19.471
- you give them a karate chop.
- I find that offensive.

00:16:19.596 --> 00:16:24.434
Just because I'm of Japanese ancestry,
you assume I know karate.

00:16:24.560 --> 00:16:28.230
Have I ever
led you to believe I have studied karate?

00:16:28.355 --> 00:16:30.941
Well, no.
But you never talk about yourself.

00:16:31.066 --> 00:16:34.570
Maybe if you showed
a little interest.

00:16:34.695 --> 00:16:36.572
Well, here goes nothing.

00:16:43.912 --> 00:16:45.914
Hello, boys.

00:16:48.083 --> 00:16:50.502
Whoa!

00:16:50.627 --> 00:16:52.921
Hyah!

00:16:54.173 --> 00:16:56.175
Aah!

00:16:56.300 --> 00:16:59.428
- There's no right way to hit a woman.
- Then do it the wrong way.

00:16:59.553 --> 00:17:02.973
Fine.
Yeee-oh-ho!

00:17:03.098 --> 00:17:06.602
Is that all you got? Hyah!

00:17:17.279 --> 00:17:18.739
- Come on, Walter!
- Take that!

00:17:20.032 --> 00:17:23.535
It hurts.

00:17:23.660 --> 00:17:27.039
Let's see if this
actually works.

00:17:27.956 --> 00:17:31.126
- Ow! Ow! Ow!
- Aah! My face!

00:17:31.251 --> 00:17:33.045
My face too!

00:17:34.087 --> 00:17:35.964
May I?

00:17:36.089 --> 00:17:37.966
Hyah!

00:17:40.135 --> 00:17:43.430
Excellent.
Excellent.

00:17:43.555 --> 00:17:47.100
Leela, please.
This is exactly what Melllvar wants.

00:17:47.226 --> 00:17:50.354
We're just pawns in his
diabolical game of checkers.

00:17:50.479 --> 00:17:53.357
Can't we resolve
our differences some other way?

00:17:53.482 --> 00:17:56.735
Melllvar!
Dinnertime!

00:17:56.860 --> 00:18:00.113
Aw, but, Mom!
I'm playin' with my collectibles!

00:18:00.280 --> 00:18:03.659
Now!

00:18:03.784 --> 00:18:07.121
All this time,
we thought he was a powerful super-being.

00:18:07.246 --> 00:18:12.209
- Yet he was just a child.
- He's not a child! He's 34!

00:18:13.669 --> 00:18:17.172
All right, Koenig!
I've wanted to do this for years!

00:18:17.297 --> 00:18:21.093
Bender, wait! This is our chance
to escape before Melllvar comes back!

00:18:21.218 --> 00:18:23.762
But we all need
to work together.

00:18:27.182 --> 00:18:30.394
- I love you so much.
- Hello.

00:18:30.519 --> 00:18:33.480
- We've decided to work together.
- Yeah, so did they.

00:18:33.605 --> 00:18:35.899
Now, how do we escape?

00:18:36.024 --> 00:18:37.901
We can't use our ship.

00:18:38.026 --> 00:18:40.154
We have life support,
but the engines are wrecked.

00:18:40.279 --> 00:18:45.033
Ironic, because our engines work,
but our life support systems don't.

00:18:45.159 --> 00:18:49.204
- Hey. If your engines work...
- And your life support systems work...

00:18:49.329 --> 00:18:51.373
Stop! You're just
goin' around in circles!

00:18:51.498 --> 00:18:54.751
Think, Fry. Think.
Everyone's depending on you.

00:19:03.385 --> 00:19:07.181
We're too heavy!
You guys need to lose some weight. Fast!

00:19:11.310 --> 00:19:13.770
Fish.

00:19:13.896 --> 00:19:16.356
Look! Leonard!
We're light enough to keep the tapes!

00:19:16.482 --> 00:19:19.943
- Isn't that great?
- I'm living in a gefilte fish jar.

00:19:23.071 --> 00:19:25.157
We did it!

00:19:30.871 --> 00:19:34.333
Melllvar's got a spaceship!

00:19:34.458 --> 00:19:36.543
Yes!
In mint condition!

00:19:36.668 --> 00:19:39.129
And you made me take it
out of the package!

00:19:45.636 --> 00:19:48.180
The Nimbus!
We're saved!

00:19:48.305 --> 00:19:52.184
You're under arrest.
Prepare to be boarded.

00:19:52.309 --> 00:19:54.978
So I boarded you, huh?
Uh, what happened next?

00:19:55.103 --> 00:19:57.189
You started this stupid
court-martial!

00:19:57.314 --> 00:19:59.483
Now if you don't mind,
we're still fighting Melllvar.

00:20:10.285 --> 00:20:13.163
One more hit, and we're done for!

00:20:13.288 --> 00:20:16.583
Let's take him out with us.
Do you guys have a self-destruct code?

00:20:16.708 --> 00:20:21.130
Like destruct sequence
1-A, 2-B, 3...

00:20:21.255 --> 00:20:24.216
Thanks a lot, Takei!
Now everybody knows!

00:20:24.341 --> 00:20:28.679
If I can't have the original
cast of Star Trek, no one will!

00:20:28.804 --> 00:20:30.681
Prepare to die!

00:20:30.806 --> 00:20:33.725
Wait! If they mean that much to you,
why do you want to kill them?

00:20:33.851 --> 00:20:36.520
Because I... I...

00:20:36.645 --> 00:20:38.730
I don't know what I'd do
without them.

00:20:38.856 --> 00:20:42.317
Melllvar, you can't
let a TV show be your whole life.

00:20:42.442 --> 00:20:45.112
You can do anything you want.
Look at Walter Koenig.

00:20:45.237 --> 00:20:47.156
After Star Trek,
he became an actor.

00:20:47.281 --> 00:20:50.325
Not just an actor
but a well-rounded person

00:20:50.451 --> 00:20:53.162
with my own friends
and credit cards and keys.

00:20:53.287 --> 00:20:57.332
Well, I... Guess I could move out
of my parents' basement.

00:20:57.458 --> 00:21:00.544
- Maybe get a temp job.
- Whoa, whoa. One step at a time.

00:21:00.669 --> 00:21:02.713
I thank you, Fry.

00:21:02.838 --> 00:21:05.507
You know, you and I
are of a kind.

00:21:05.632 --> 00:21:09.261
In a different reality,
I could have called you... Friend.

00:21:09.386 --> 00:21:12.222
Episode 10.
"Balance of Terror."

00:21:12.347 --> 00:21:14.516
More like episode nine,
loser!

00:21:14.641 --> 00:21:17.144
In your face!
Victory is mine!

00:21:20.522 --> 00:21:22.441
I wonder, my friends.

00:21:22.566 --> 00:21:25.235
Was he really such
an evil energy gas?

00:21:25.360 --> 00:21:27.696
He did give us
eternal youth.

00:21:27.821 --> 00:21:29.698
Twenty-four hour
laundromat.

00:21:29.823 --> 00:21:33.911
A full assortment of rum,
both spiced and regular.

00:21:34.036 --> 00:21:36.163
Truly,
it was a paradise.

00:21:36.288 --> 00:21:40.334
And all you had to put up with was
one really annoying Star Trek fan.

00:21:41.502 --> 00:21:43.337
Let's get the hell
out of here.